  "summary_en": "European Commission Communication presenting an EU approach to online child safety, accompanying the proposed EU KIDS Act. It sets minimum ages for social media, safe-design duties (including for AI chatbots and companions), age verification and enforcement, plus complementary measures on consumer law, education and international cooperation.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "EU KIDS Act proposes EU-wide minimum age: no social media under 13, own accounts from 15, parent-supervised mini accounts at 13-15",
   "Safe-design duties: no addictive features, regulated recommender systems, safe default settings, no unwanted contacts",
   "Covers 'Social Media+' including AI chatbots and companions via co-regulatory, industry-led commitments",
   "Mandatory age verification using EU age verification tool; app stores must apply age ratings",
   "Enforcement builds on DSA and AI Act with independent audits of compliance plans and a supervisory fee"
  ],
